#
# The public SSH key that signs OAK Community releases from 1.0.0 on (RR-005), in the
# `ssh-keygen -Y` allowed-signers format: one line, `<principal> <key type> <public key>`.
# `scripts/verify_release.py` checks `SHA256SUMS.sig` against this file and nothing else.
#
# No key is pinned yet: the maintainer generates the key, keeps the private half offline
# and adds the public line here when cutting 1.0.0 (docs/release-process.md). Until then
# a release from 1.0.0 on cannot verify, which is the point.
